// The Node harnesses under packages/*/*/harness/, typechecked separately from
// everything else.
//
// This is the one split in the TypeScript config, and it is not a per-package
// one: tsconfig.json describes browser code, and browser code must not be able
// to see `process`, `node:fs`, or anything else Node hands out — a shell that
// compiles against those does not run on a page. Merging the two would put
// Node's globals in scope for the whole tree, which is exactly the leak the
// package boundaries exist to prevent.
//
// Everything else is inherited, strict flags included. Run it through
// `cargo xtask check`, never directly: the generated glue the harnesses import
// does not exist until the wasm is built.
{
	"extends": "./tsconfig.json",
	"compilerOptions": {
		"types": ["node"]
	},
	"include": [
		"packages/*/*/harness/**/*.ts",
		"packages/base/boundary/generated/*.d.ts"
	]
}
